{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat ../research.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"audit_spec_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_20-01-28-etcd_raft-real-run/audit-spec/v1.json\",\n  \"audit_spec_version\": 1,\n  \"activity_roles\": {\n    \"A1\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Qualified support for decision formation and legal advancement\"\n    },\n    \"A2\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Context validity and acquisition, transfer or loss of authority\"\n    },\n    \"A3\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Recovery and resynchronization of eligible participation\"\n    },\n    \"A4\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Configuration and participant eligibility\"\n    },\n    \"A5\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Decision application and consumption\"\n    },\n    \"A6\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"History, persistence and reconstruction of support\"\n    },\n    \"A7\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Client contracts, invocation intervals and observed completion\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"activity_focus\": [],\n  \"understanding_status\": \"usable\",\n  \"core_overview\": {\n    \"formation\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"A leader assigns term/index to proposals, emits log appends and defers its self-ack until persistence. Followers check predecessor identity, preserve committed entries, append the uncommitted suffix and return durability-dependent support. In the leader term, known-peer positive replies update Match; voting majority (both halves if joint) yields a candidate index, and matching the current term permits committed advancement. Broadcast append and Match-capped heartbeat propagate the decision. Ready then exposes the ordered committed prefix subject to snapshot and local-stability/application-size constraints; caller application and acknowledgment consume it. Rejection hints, heartbeat-driven empty appends and snapshot fallback support recovery without treating activity as matched history.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-formation\",\n        \"B-follow-log\",\n        \"B-persistence\",\n        \"B-application\",\n        \"B-config\",\n        \"B-recovery\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-match\",\n        \"F-commit\",\n        \"F-config\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"M-advance\",\n        \"M-api\",\n        \"M-apply-response\",\n        \"M-async-contract\",\n        \"M-auto\",\n        \"M-auto-contract\",\n        \"M-bootstrap\",\n        \"M-changer\",\n        \"M-changer-roles\",\n        \"M-conf-contract\",\n        \"M-conf-conversion\",\n        \"M-conf-restore\",\n        \"M-config\",\n        \"M-dispatch\",\n        \"M-follower-log\",\n        \"M-init\",\n        \"M-joint-quorum\",\n        \"M-log-append\",\n        \"M-log-apply\",\n        \"M-log-commit\",\n        \"M-log-pointers\",\n        \"M-majority\",\n        \"M-memory-storage\",\n        \"M-node-loop\",\n        \"M-proposal\",\n        \"M-ready\",\n        \"M-replicate\",\n        \"M-reset\",\n        \"M-restore\",\n        \"M-send\",\n        \"M-storage-contract\",\n        \"M-storage-response\",\n        \"M-support\",\n        \"M-tracker\",\n        \"M-unstable\",\n        \"M-unstable-replace\",\n        \"M-votes\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"context\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Election starts only from a promotable instance with no committed unapplied configuration. PreVote probes without raising term; real campaign increments term and counts persisted self/peer votes using current voter sets and log freshness. Higher-term dispatch or loss of quorum can relinquish authority; same-term leader traffic demotes candidates. Reset clears transient vote/read/peer-progress state but retains log and committed decisions. Older network replies are rejected; append-storage completions are term-qualified, whereas committed snapshot/apply completions survive term changes. Leadership transfer first catches up a tracked voter, then sends TimeoutNow and suppresses proposals until takeover or timeout.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-authority\",\n        \"B-transfer\",\n        \"B-persistence\",\n        \"B-recovery\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-authority\",\n        \"F-config\",\n        \"F-commit\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"M-advance\",\n        \"M-apply-response\",\n        \"M-async-contract\",\n        \"M-auto-contract\",\n        \"M-bootstrap\",\n        \"M-changer\",\n        \"M-conf-contract\",\n        \"M-conf-restore\",\n        \"M-config\",\n        \"M-dispatch\",\n        \"M-election\",\n        \"M-follower-log\",\n        \"M-init\",\n        \"M-log-append\",\n        \"M-log-commit\",\n        \"M-memory-storage\",\n        \"M-proposal\",\n        \"M-ready\",\n        \"M-reset\",\n        \"M-restore\",\n        \"M-role-handlers\",\n        \"M-send\",\n        \"M-storage-contract\",\n        \"M-storage-response\",\n        \"M-transfer\",\n        \"M-transfer-abort\",\n        \"M-unstable\",\n        \"M-unstable-replace\",\n        \"M-votes\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"connection\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"A2 qualifies whose A1 support can be consumed: term dispatch and reset prevent a new leader from aggregating old-term replication replies, and the current-term entry requirement ties retained older log history to fresh quorum support. Committed decisions are term-independent, so application/storage snapshot acknowledgment may complete after leadership changes; overwritable append history instead needs a current-term durability attestation. Applied configuration changes alter the voter sets used by both election and replication quorums, while campaign blocks unapplied committed membership. Automatic joint exit is a separate application-triggered proposal, so recorded AutoLeave and recorded application do not themselves mean exit was scheduled. Pending read-only acknowledgments reset with authority; the pre-current-term request queue survives reset and is reprocessed through current-term read logic on an append-response commit.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-authority\",\n        \"B-formation\",\n        \"B-persistence\",\n        \"B-config\",\n        \"B-auto-leave\",\n        \"B-application\",\n        \"B-client-read\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-authority\",\n        \"F-match\",\n        \"F-commit\",\n        \"F-config\",\n        \"F-applied\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"M-advance\",\n        \"M-api\",\n        \"M-apply-response\",\n        \"M-async-contract\",\n        \"M-auto\",\n        \"M-auto-contract\",\n        \"M-bootstrap\",\n        \"M-changer\",\n        \"M-changer-roles\",\n        \"M-conf-contract\",\n        \"M-conf-conversion\",\n        \"M-conf-restore\",\n        \"M-config\",\n        \"M-dispatch\",\n        \"M-election\",\n        \"M-follower-log\",\n        \"M-init\",\n        \"M-joint-quorum\",\n        \"M-log-append\",\n        \"M-log-apply\",\n        \"M-log-commit\",\n        \"M-log-pointers\",\n        \"M-majority\",\n        \"M-node-loop\",\n        \"M-pending-read\",\n        \"M-proposal\",\n        \"M-read\",\n        \"M-read-tracker\",\n        \"M-ready\",\n        \"M-replicate\",\n        \"M-reset\",\n        \"M-role-handlers\",\n        \"M-send\",\n        \"M-storage-response\",\n        \"M-support\",\n        \"M-tracker\",\n        \"M-unstable\",\n        \"M-unstable-replace\",\n        \"M-votes\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"open_details\": [\n      \"Whether automatic leave can lose its continuation when transfer suppresses the final application-triggered attempt and later times out.\",\n      \"Whether configuration-triggered commitment can be the first current-term commit with pending reads, despite campaign restrictions.\",\n      \"Early-Advance configuration ordering, detailed membership/removal read interactions, and broader concurrent snapshot/apply histories remain uninvestigated variants.\"\n    ],\n    \"core_gaps\": [],\n    \"status\": \"usable\",\n    \"rationale\": \"Representative formation and authority paths were traced through producers, quorum aggregation, persistence, dispatch, configuration, recovery and application. This is a navigable initial explanation, not full path coverage or defect evidence.\"\n  },\n  \"understanding_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"operation_id\": \"4c727c61599b4106adba0a66ddb56f7a\",\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"selections\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"operation_id\": \"4c727c61599b4106adba0a66ddb56f7a\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"next_objective\": {\n    \"action\": \"investigate_and_refocus\",\n    \"boundary\": \"both_core_paths\",\n    \"reason\": \"Use results to update understanding and compare the remaining frontier\",\n    \"core_gaps\": []\n  },\n  \"drafts\": [],\n  \"candidates\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c1ba7e9ff9034a728850b297376ecbb8\",\n      \"question\": {\n        \"audit_spec_version\": 1,\n        \"disposition\": \"concrete_suspicion\",\n        \"preferred_check\": \"controlled_schedule\",\n        \"question\": \"When an applied implicit-joint configuration requests automatic exit, can leadership transfer reject the last application-triggered leave proposal and then time out while the same leader remains healthy, with no implementation-owned continuation to propose exit in an otherwise idle cluster?\",\n        \"importance\": \"A lost configuration-completion continuation can retain outgoing voters and joint quorum requirements after removal/replacement was requested, obstructing subsequent configuration changes and reducing availability. This is a scoped progress concern; no consensus-safety violation is presumed.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"M-conf-contract\",\n          \"M-auto-contract\",\n          \"M-auto\",\n          \"M-proposal\",\n          \"M-election\",\n          \"M-transfer-abort\",\n          \"M-apply-response\",\n          \"M-advance\",\n          \"M-api\",\n          \"M-auto-test\"\n        ],\n        \"participants\": [\n          \"Current leader\",\n          \"Voting transferee\",\n          \"Other voters in old/new configurations\",\n          \"Ready caller\"\n        ],\n        \"objects\": [\n          \"Active implicit-joint configuration\",\n          \"Automatically generated zero ConfChangeV2 proposal\",\n          \"leadTransferee\",\n          \"Application acknowledgment\"\n        ],\n        \"contexts\": [\n          \"Same retained leader term after a bounded failed leadership transfer\",\n          \"Configuration genuinely committed and applied before acknowledgment\",\n          \"Reliable ongoing heartbeat/Ready processing after bounded transport loss, no unrelated client proposal\"\n        ],\n        \"event_paths\": [\n          \"ProposeConfChange -> commit -> Ready.CommittedEntries -> ApplyConfChange -> transfer begins -> Advance -> appliedTo -> MsgProp rejected\",\n          \"Tick -> transfer timeout -> abortLeaderTransfer -> heartbeat-only Ready/Advance\"\n        ],\n        \"activity_classes\": [\n          \"A4\",\n          \"A1\",\n          \"A2\"\n        ],\n        \"behavior_ids\": [\n          \"B-config\",\n          \"B-auto-leave\"\n        ],\n        \"fact_ids\": [\n          \"F-config\"\n        ],\n        \"supporting_behavior_ids\": {\n          \"B-transfer\": \"Produces and removes the proposal blocker without itself creating application work.\",\n          \"B-application\": \"Determines whether Ready/Advance actually produces the next appliedTo trigger.\",\n          \"B-formation\": \"Commits joint entry under actual voter quorums; a later unrelated proposal is a possible rescue, not yet an established caller duty.\",\n          \"B-authority\": \"Successful transfer or later election provides an alternative leader/no-op/application path.\"\n        },\n        \"obligation_relation_kind\": \"consumption\",\n        \"counterevidence\": [\n          \"appliedTo retries on later applied entries; a successful transfer/new leader can append and apply a no-op.\",\n          \"Transfer timeout is bounded by electionTimeout and ordinary proposals are admitted after abort.\",\n          \"Existing TestRawNodeJointAutoLeave expects recovery after leadership loss and reelection, but does not test failed transfer with the same idle leader; parts of that test explicitly pretend a config applied, so it is not a legal-history driver to reuse unexamined.\",\n          \"Caller proposals may be dropped, and their retries are external. Need distinguish that from the documented AutoLeave continuation once the entering configuration was already committed/applied.\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"Construct a legal Ready/application history that overlaps transfer with the final application acknowledgment without excluding the relevant overlap or fabricating peer support.\",\n          \"Determine whether periodic ticks, real message delivery and empty Ready/Advance cycles generate a later application trigger after all entering-config work drains.\",\n          \"Ground any progress oracle in automatic proposal continuation, not an invented numeric deadline; a finite no-exit window alone cannot establish infinite stalling.\"\n        ],\n        \"priority\": 2,\n        \"trigger_rationale\": \"The explicit comment at appliedTo promises retry on next advance after failed transfer, but acceptReady queues an apply response only for nonempty committed entries and abortLeaderTransfer only clears its field. Contract/source reading supplies a concrete discriminator. A controlled real-node schedule can distinguish hidden continuation from reliance on later unrelated application. This is more informative than rerunning the explained obsolete-storage-response term guard; the configuration-commit/read-release lead needs more legal-history source work before execution.\"\n      },\n      \"status\": \"active\",\n      \"parent_candidate_id\": null,\n      \"fork_reason\": \"\",\n      \"stop_reason\": \"Register initial sourced core map and one focused automatic-configuration-continuation question. No violation, obligation or execution result is asserted.\",\n      \"resume_conditions\": [],\n      \"obligation_id\": null,\n      \"result_claim_ids\": [],\n      \"open_issue_ids\": [],\n      \"executions\": [],\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"question_candidates\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"id\": \"c1ba7e9ff9034a728850b297376ecbb8\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"units\": [],\n  \"claims\": [],\n  \"artifacts\": [],\n  \"assessments\": [],\n  \"frontier\": {\n    \"relationships\": [\n      {\n        \"fact_id\": \"F-authority\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"M-election\",\n          \"M-dispatch\",\n          \"M-reset\",\n          \"M-init\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [],\n        \"producers\": [\n          \"B-authority\"\n        ],\n        \"consumers\": [\n          \"B-transfer\",\n          \"B-formation\",\n          \"B-follow-log\",\n          \"B-persistence\",\n          \"B-config\",\n          \"B-auto-leave\",\n          \"B-client-read\"\n        ],\n        \"invalidators\": [\n          \"B-authority\",\n          \"B-config\",\n          \"B-recovery\"\n        ],\n        \"reinterpreters\": [],\n        \"unreferenced_behavior_ids\": [\n          \"B-authority\",\n          \"B-auto-leave\",\n          \"B-client-read\",\n          \"B-config\",\n          \"B-follow-log\",\n          \"B-formation\",\n          \"B-per